SUMMARY:Volunteer at AVL Sounds Fest
DESCRIPTION:AVL Digital Nomads\nAVL Digital Nomads is supporting two venue
 s at AVL Sounds Fest\, and we need you.\nAVL Sounds Fest is Asheville's ci
 tywide music festival: August 6–9\, more than 240 artists across 17 stag
 es\, from The Orange Peel and The Grey Eagle to brand-new outdoor rooms li
 ke this one. It's the festival's first year back after Hurricane Helene fo
 rced the 2025 hiatus\, and a portion of proceeds goes to the WNC Long Haul
  – Recovery and Resilience Fund.\nWe've claimed Asheville Yards on Frida
 y and Hellbender on Sunday.\nThis event is Friday.\n**THE SHIFT** 📅 Fri
 day\, August 7 🕐 [SHIFT WINDOW — 5 hours] 📍 Asheville Yards\, 🌤
  Outdoor venue\nMusic runs 2:00 PM to 11:00 PM that day: Erick Baker\, Cai
 tlin Krisko & The Broadcast\, Grace Bowers\, Toubab Krewe\, Big Freedia at
  8:00\, and Preservation Hall Jazz Band closing it out at 9:30.\n**WHAT YO
 U GET**\nThe festival gives volunteers who work **two 5-hour shifts**:\n
 🎟 A weekend festival pass — all four days\, every venue (passes retai
 l at $161.50) 👕 An AVL Sounds Fest volunteer T-shirt 🎉 An invite to 
 the volunteer party\n**Read that again: the weekend pass takes TWO shifts.
 ** One shift here on Friday plus one at Hellbender on Sunday gets you ther
 e. OR\, two on Friday works too.\nSign up for both: 👉 Sunday at Hellben
 der: https://www.meetup.com/avl-digital-nomads/events/315867475/?slug=avl-
 digital-nomads&eventId=315867475\n**WHAT YOU'LL ACTUALLY DO**\nThe festiva
 l assigns roles at check-in from its standard list: Wristband Checker\, Ti
 cketing\, Venue Ambassador\, Merch\, Stage Manager\, MC\, Floater\, and VI
 P. Most of our crew will land on wristbands\, ticketing\, and ambassador w
 ork — checking passes\, keeping the entry line moving\, and answering "w
 hat's playing next door?"\nNo experience needed. Everything gets a walkthr
 ough on-site before doors.\n**WEAR AND BRING**\n\n* Closed-toe shoes. You'
 ll be on pavement for five hours.\n* A refillable water bottle. Outdoor ve
 nue\, August\, evening sun.\n* Sunscreen and a light rain layer — aftern
 oon thunderstorms are normal here.\n* Photo ID and a charged phone.\n\n**R
 SVP here on Meetup.** We will coordinate with AVL Sounds Fest.
