SUMMARY:Volunteer at AVL Sounds Fest
DESCRIPTION:AVL Digital Nomads\nAVL Digital Nomads is supporting two venue
 s at AVL Sounds Fest. This is the Sunday shift\, and it's the one with Dr.
  Dog.\nAVL Sounds Fest is Asheville's citywide music festival: August 6–
 9\, more than 240 artists on 17 stages across the city. It's the first yea
 r back after Hurricane Helene forced the 2025 hiatus\, and a portion of pr
 oceeds goes to the WNC Long Haul – Recovery and Resilience Fund.\nHellbe
 nder is The Orange Peel's brand-new outdoor venue\, and this is its first 
 festival.\n**THE SHIFT** 📅 Sunday\, August 9 — closing day 🕐 [SHIF
 T WINDOW — 5 hours] 📍 Hellbender\,\n🌤 Outdoor venue\nMusic that da
 y: Tyler Ramsey & Carl Broemel of My Morning Jacket at 2:00\, Floating Act
 ion at 3:45\, and **Dr. Dog at 5:30** — their only announced show of 202
 6\, with Asheville-resident frontman Scott McMicken coming home for it.\n*
 *WHAT YOU GET**\nThe festival gives volunteers who work **two 5-hour shift
 s**:\n🎟 A weekend festival pass — all four days\, every venue ($161.5
 0 retail)\n👕 An AVL Sounds Fest volunteer T-shirt\n🎉 An invite to th
 e volunteer party\n**The pass takes TWO shifts.** Pair this one with our F
 riday shift at Asheville Yards and you're covered:\n👉 Friday at Ashevil
 le Yards: https://www.meetup.com/avl-digital-nomads/events/315867364/?even
 tOrigin=group_events_list&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=event_card_save
 devents_share_modal&utm_source=link&utm_version=v2&member_id=209607837\n\n
 **WHAT YOU'LL ACTUALLY DO**\nRoles are assigned at check-in from the festi
 val's list: Wristband Checker\, Ticketing\, Venue Ambassador\, Merch\, Sta
 ge Manager\, MC\, Floater\, VIP. Expect most of us on wristbands\, ticketi
 ng\, and ambassador work.\nHeads up on this one: Dr. Dog at 5:30 means a h
 eavy arrival wave between roughly 4:30 and 5:30 at a venue that's brand ne
 w. That hour is the job. It's also the best hour of the weekend to be stan
 ding at that gate.\nNo experience needed. Full walkthrough before doors.\n
 **WEAR AND BRING**\n\n* Closed-toe shoes\, no exceptions.\n* A refillable 
 water bottle. Afternoon shift\, direct August sun.\n* Sunscreen and a hat.
  Seriously.\n* A light rain layer.\n* Photo ID and a charged phone.\n\n**G
 ETTING THERE**\nHellbender is south of downtown on Thompson. Plan your par
 king before you arrive.
