SUMMARY:AVL UX
DESCRIPTION:AVL Digital Nomads\n**AVL UX is back. Same energy\, even more 
 momentum.**\n\n**Description:**\n\nThe first meetup made one thing clear: 
 **Asheville has more UX\, product\, research\, and designers than we usual
 ly get to see in one room.**\nSo for event two\, we’re getting into how 
 real product problems are actually solved.\n\nThis time\, **Aktiga’s *Ra
 chel Stickels* will share about an ongoing project** to support Western No
 rth Carolina’s only homeless day center. We’ll get a behind-the-scenes
  view into their research methods and collaborative design process\, follo
 wed by a Q&A.\n\n**What to Expect:**\n\n* Quick welcome and casual network
 ing.\n* A 30 minute keynote from Aktiga.\n* Audience Q&A.\n* Drinks\, name
  tags\, and networking afterward.\n\n**Who's welcome?**\n\nEVERYONE!\nDesi
 gners\, researchers\, product managers\, developers\, founders\, students\
 , career-switchers\, and anyone curious about UX or how products are shape
 d and built.\nCome with questions. **Meet more of Asheville’s UX communi
 ty.** Leave with new connections\, practical ideas\, and a clearer look at
  where this community could go next.\n\n**Details**\n\n* Date: Thursday\, 
 August 27th 2026\n* Time: 6:00–8:00 PM\n* Venue: 7 Acres Coworking- 105 
 Fairview Rd\, Asheville\, NC 28803\n* Cost: Free\n* Check out the sponsors
  [Aktiga](https://aktiga.com/)!
